  "created": "2026-06-20T17:06:28.99Z",
  "description": "Standalone MQTT nodes for FluxFlow over small injected MQTT contracts: IMqttPublisher for publish, IMqttTriggerSource for trigger subscriptions, and optional IMqttClientHealthSource health. Includes trigger request/reply acknowledgement through a correlated response port. Broadcast output/error/event ports. No engine or concrete MQTT client required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Mqtt",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-20T17:09:35.107Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "Ly3yfkg9yY/bRIJNm8sxNvXPkf0OHfI60ZJ2C7XIb7lg1b3Aex2No8s9I1/o7htUCQzosQdXp9Z5+Qok1P0kGg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 65174,
  "published": "2026-06-20T17:06:28.99Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking cleanup of the MQTT component boundary. The core package now exposes only client-library-neutral publish, trigger, health, received-context, and protocol metadata contracts. Publish and trigger nodes no longer own connection handles, factories, profiles, reconnect policy, concrete client creation, or client lifetime. MqttPublishOptions now contains only node runtime settings; publish topic, quality-of-service, retain flag, payload, and MQTT protocol metadata live on MqttPublishRequest. Trigger request/reply uses CorrelatedRequestTracker for pending correlation and timeout mechanics while acknowledgement policy stays MQTT-owned. Concrete client-library integrations are split into separate adapter packages.",
